--
-- Tests for bc-interpretation-reading.l4 (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, ss 2(2), 2(3), 6, 7, 8,
-- 8.1(2), 8.1(3), 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 15, 28(2) to (4), 30, 31, 33(2) to (6), 39, 40, 42(1), 43, 44).
-- Each expected value was decided from the text before the file was first run. Every limb of a rule is tested on both
-- sides; where the text does not answer, the test asserts the named refusal and its message.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-definitions`
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-reading`

§ `s 2(2) and s 2(3)`

-- s 2(2): "The provisions of this Act apply to this Act."
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the provisions of this Act apply to the enactment` `This Act`
-- The text does not say how the provisions apply to another enactment: that is s 2(1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(2) the provisions of this Act apply to the enactment` `Another enactment`
        BECAUSE "s 2(2) speaks only of this Act; s 2(1) governs another enactment"

-- s 2(3): a rule of construction "applicable to it and not inconsistent with this Act" is not excluded.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` TRUE FALSE
-- A rule that is not applicable, or is inconsistent with this Act, is outside what the sentence preserves; it does not say such a rule is excluded.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 2(3) speaks only of a rule of construction that is applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with this Act"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` FALSE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 2(3) speaks only of a rule of construction that is applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with this Act"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(3) a rule of construction is preserved by this Act` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 2(3) speaks only of a rule of construction that is applicable to the enactment and not inconsistent with this Act"

§ `s 6 Private Acts`

-- "A provision in a private Act does not affect the rights of any person, except only as referred to or mentioned in that Act."
#ASSERT `s 6 what a provision in an Act does to a person's right` `A private Act` FALSE EQUALS `The provision does not affect the right`
#ASSERT `s 6 what a provision in an Act does to a person's right` `A private Act` TRUE EQUALS `The provision affects the right only as the Act refers to or mentions it`
-- The section says nothing of an Act that is not private.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 6 what a provision in an Act does to a person's right` `Any other Act` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 6 speaks only of a provision in a private Act"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 6 what a provision in an Act does to a person's right` `Any other Act` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 6 speaks only of a provision in a private Act"

§ `s 7 Always speaking`

-- 7 (1): "Every enactment must be construed as always speaking": read it as of the day it is applied, not the day it was enacted.
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the day as of which an enactment is read` (YMD 1996 6 1) (YMD 2026 10 29) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 29
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7(1) the day as of which an enactment is read` (YMD 1996 6 1) (YMD 2026 10 29) EQUALS YMD 1996 6 1)

-- 7 (2): a provision "expressed in the present tense" applies "to the circumstances as they arise".
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` `Present tense` TRUE
-- The text does not say what happens to a circumstance that arises while the enactment is not in force.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7(2) the provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` `Present tense` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 7(2) does not say whether a provision applies to a circumstance that arises while the enactment is not in force"
-- A provision not in the present tense is not within the sentence.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7(2) the provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` `Another tense` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 7(2) speaks only of a provision expressed in the present tense"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7(2) the provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` `Another tense` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 7(2) speaks only of a provision expressed in the present tense"

§ `s 8 Remedial`

-- "such fair, large and liberal construction and interpretation as best ensures the attainment of its objects": the
-- judgment of which construction does that is an input.
#ASSERT `s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` (LIST `A candidate construction` "narrow" FALSE, `A candidate construction` "purposive" TRUE) EQUALS "purposive"
#ASSERT `s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` (LIST `A candidate construction` "purposive" TRUE, `A candidate construction` "narrow" FALSE) EQUALS "purposive"
#ASSERT `s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` (LIST `A candidate construction` "only" TRUE) EQUALS "only"
-- Neither candidate best ensures the attainment of the objects: the section names no construction.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` (LIST `A candidate construction` "a" FALSE, `A candidate construction` "b" FALSE)
        BECAUSE "s 8 names no construction when none is said to best ensure the attainment of the objects"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` EMPTY
        BECAUSE "s 8 names no construction when none is said to best ensure the attainment of the objects"
-- Two candidates both said to best ensure the attainment of the objects: the section does not choose between them.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8 the construction to give to an enactment` (LIST `A candidate construction` "a" TRUE, `A candidate construction` "b" TRUE)
        BECAUSE "s 8 does not choose between constructions that equally best ensure the attainment of the objects"

§ `s 8.1(2) and (3)`

-- 8.1 (2): "every enactment must be construed as upholding and not abrogating or derogating from" s 35 rights.
#ASSERT `s 8.1(2) a construction of an enactment is open` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8.1(2) a construction of an enactment is open` TRUE)

-- 8.1 (3): "Every Act and regulation must be construed as being consistent with the Declaration."
#ASSERT `s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` `An Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` `An Act` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` `A regulation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` `A regulation` FALSE)
-- Some other kind of enactment (a bylaw, an order) is not in the sentence.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` `An enactment that is neither an Act nor a regulation` TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 8.1(3) speaks only of an Act and a regulation"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 8.1(3) a construction of the enactment is open` `An enactment that is neither an Act nor a regulation` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 8.1(3) speaks only of an Act and a regulation"

§ `s 9 and s 11 What is part of an enactment`

-- s 9: "The title and preamble of an enactment are part of it and are intended to assist in explaining its meaning and object."
#ASSERT `s 9 the part is part of the enactment` `The title`
#ASSERT `s 9 the part is part of the enactment` `The preamble`
#ASSERT `s 9 the part is intended to assist in explaining the meaning and object of the enactment` `The title`
#ASSERT `s 9 the part is intended to assist in explaining the meaning and object of the enactment` `The preamble`
-- A head note is for s 11, not s 9.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 9 the part is part of the enactment` `A head note to a provision`
        BECAUSE "s 9 speaks only of the title and the preamble"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 9 the part is intended to assist in explaining the meaning and object of the enactment` `Any other part`
        BECAUSE "s 9 speaks only of the title and the preamble"

-- s 11 (1): a head note, and a reference after the end of a section or other division, "is not part of the enactment" and
-- "must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only".
#ASSERT NOT (`s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `A head note to a provision`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `A reference after the end of a section or other division`)
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) the part must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only` `A head note to a provision`
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) the part must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only` `A reference after the end of a section or other division`
-- s 11 (2): "italicized text in square brackets that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"
-- after "a reference to a provision of the enactment or any other enactment" is treated as (1)(a) and (b) treat the head note.
#ASSERT `s 11(2) subsection (1)(a) and (b) apply to the text in square brackets` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Each of the three conditions is the (2) sentence's antecedent: with any one missing the sentence says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(2) subsection (1)(a) and (b) apply to the text in square brackets` FALSE TRUE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(2) subsection (1)(a) and (b) apply to the text in square brackets` TRUE FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(2) subsection (1)(a) and (b) apply to the text in square brackets` TRUE TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` (`Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `s 11(1)(b) the part must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only` (`Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` TRUE TRUE)
-- Square-bracket text that is not italicized, or not descriptive, is not covered by s 11(2); the Act does not say what it is.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` (`Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` FALSE TRUE)
        BECAUSE "s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` (`Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` TRUE FALSE)
        BECAUSE "s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(1)(b) the part must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only` (`Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` FALSE FALSE)
        BECAUSE "s 11(2) speaks only of italicized text in square brackets, after a reference to a provision, that is or purports to be descriptive of the subject matter of the provision"
-- The title is not within s 11(1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `The title`
        BECAUSE "s 11(1) speaks only of a head note, a reference after the end of a section or division, and text in square brackets"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11(1)(b) the part must be considered to have been added editorially for convenience of reference only` `Any other part`
        BECAUSE "s 11(1) speaks only of a head note, a reference after the end of a section or division, and text in square brackets"

-- The two sections read together.
#ASSERT `s 9 and s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `The title`
#ASSERT `s 9 and s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `The preamble`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9 and s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `A head note to a provision`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9 and s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `A reference after the end of a section or other division`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9 and s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` (`Text in square brackets after a reference to a provision` TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 9 and s 11(1)(a) the part is part of the enactment` `Any other part`
        BECAUSE "s 11(1) speaks only of a head note, a reference after the end of a section or division, and text in square brackets"

§ `s 10 Enacting clause`

-- The form the text gives.
#ASSERT `the form of enacting clause that s 10 gives` EQUALS "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Legislative Assembly of the Province of British Columbia, enacts as follows:"
#ASSERT `s 10 the enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in this form` "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Legislative Assembly of the Province of British Columbia, enacts as follows:"
-- "may be in the following form" does not say another form is forbidden (fork F-open-list).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10 the enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in this form` "Be it enacted by the Legislature of the Province of British Columbia:"
        BECAUSE "s 10 says only that the enacting clause of an Act may be in the form given; it does not say that another form is not allowed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 10 the enacting clause of an Act of the Legislature may be in this form` ""
        BECAUSE "s 10 says only that the enacting clause of an Act may be in the form given; it does not say that another form is not allowed"

§ `s 12 Definitions apply to the whole enactment`

-- "unless the contrary intention appears in the enactment, apply to the whole enactment including the section containing a definition"
#ASSERT `s 12 the definition or interpretation provision applies in the place` `In the section containing the definition or interpretation provision` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12 the definition or interpretation provision applies in the place` `In the section containing the definition or interpretation provision` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 12 the definition or interpretation provision applies in the place` `In another part of the enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 12 the definition or interpretation provision applies in the place` `In another part of the enactment` TRUE)
-- The section does not carry a definition into another enactment.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 12 the definition or interpretation provision applies in the place` `In another enactment` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 12 speaks only of the enactment that contains the definition or interpretation provision"

§ `s 13 Expressions in regulations`

-- "An expression used in a regulation has the same meaning as in the enactment authorizing the regulation."
#ASSERT `s 13 the meaning of an expression used in a regulation` (JUST "a thing the Act defines") EQUALS JUST "a thing the Act defines"
-- The authorizing enactment does not use the expression: s 13 gives it no meaning.
#ASSERT `s 13 the meaning of an expression used in a regulation` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 15 Power of repeal and amendment`

-- 15 (1): "reserve to the Legislature the power of repealing or amending it, and of revoking, restricting or modifying a power, privilege or advantage"
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the Act is construed as reserving to the Legislature the power` `Repeal it`
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the Act is construed as reserving to the Legislature the power` `Amend it`
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the Act is construed as reserving to the Legislature the power` `Revoke a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person`
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the Act is construed as reserving to the Legislature the power` `Restrict a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person`
#ASSERT `s 15(1) the Act is construed as reserving to the Legislature the power` `Modify a power, privilege or advantage that it vests in or grants to a person`
-- 15 (2): "An Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session of the Legislature."
#ASSERT `s 15(2) an Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session` TRUE
-- (2) says nothing of an Act passed in a later session: (1) reserves the power, so that is not a "no".
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 15(2) an Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session` FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 15(2) speaks only of an Act passed in the same session of the Legislature; s 15(1) reserves the power generally"

§ `s 28 Use of words`

-- 28 (2): "Gender specific terms include all genders and include corporations."
#ASSERT `s 28(2) a gender specific term includes` `A person of any gender`
#ASSERT `s 28(2) a gender specific term includes` `A corporation`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 28(2) a gender specific term includes` `Something that is neither a person nor a corporation`
        BECAUSE "s 28(2) speaks only of persons of any gender and corporations"

-- 28 (3): "words in the singular include the plural, and words in the plural include the singular."
#ASSERT `s 28(3) a word in one number includes the other number` `Singular` `Plural`
#ASSERT `s 28(3) a word in one number includes the other number` `Plural` `Singular`
#ASSERT `s 28(3) a word in one number includes the other number` `Singular` `Singular`
#ASSERT `s 28(3) a word in one number includes the other number` `Plural` `Plural`

-- 28 (4): "If a word or expression is defined in an enactment, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the same word
-- or expression have corresponding meanings."
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the form has a corresponding meaning` TRUE TRUE
-- With either condition missing the sentence is not engaged.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 28(4) the form has a corresponding meaning` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 28(4) speaks only of another part of speech or grammatical form of a word or expression defined in the enactment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 28(4) the form has a corresponding meaning` TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 28(4) speaks only of another part of speech or grammatical form of a word or expression defined in the enactment"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 28(4) the form has a corresponding meaning` FALSE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 28(4) speaks only of another part of speech or grammatical form of a word or expression defined in the enactment"

§ `s 30 Metric expressions`

-- "have the meaning given to them in the Weights and Measures Act (Canada) and if not mentioned there, have the meaning
-- given to them in the International System of Units"
#ASSERT `s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` (JUST "from the Weights and Measures Act") (JUST "from the SI") EQUALS "from the Weights and Measures Act"
#ASSERT `s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` (JUST "from the Weights and Measures Act") NOTHING EQUALS "from the Weights and Measures Act"
#ASSERT `s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` NOTHING (JUST "from the SI") EQUALS "from the SI"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 30 the meaning of a metric expression or symbol` NOTHING NOTHING
        BECAUSE "s 30 gives no meaning to a metric expression that neither the Weights and Measures Act (Canada) nor the International System of Units gives a meaning to"

§ `s 31 Common names`

-- "the name commonly applied to a ... thing means the ... thing to which the name is commonly applied, although the name is not the formal or extended designation of it."
#ASSERT `s 31 what the commonly applied name means` "the Dominion" "Canada" "the Dominion of Canada" EQUALS "Canada"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31 what the commonly applied name means` "the Dominion" "Canada" "the Dominion of Canada" EQUALS "the Dominion of Canada")

§ `s 33 References in enactments`

-- 33 (2): a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference to one of "the enactment in which the reference occurs".
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A Part` "the Land Title Act" EQUALS "the Land Title Act"
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A division` "the Land Title Act" EQUALS "the Land Title Act"
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A section` "the Land Title Act" EQUALS "the Land Title Act"
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A schedule` "the Land Title Act" EQUALS "the Land Title Act"
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `An appendix` "the Land Title Act" EQUALS "the Land Title Act"
#ASSERT `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A form` "the Land Title Act" EQUALS "the Land Title Act"
-- (2) names six things; a subsection is (3)'s.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A subsection` "the Land Title Act"
        BECAUSE "s 33(2) speaks only of a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 33(2) the enactment a reference to a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is a reference into` `A clause` "the Land Title Act"
        BECAUSE "s 33(2) speaks only of a Part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form"

-- 33 (3): a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is one "of the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph in which the reference occurs".
#ASSERT `s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` `A subsection` `In a section` EQUALS `In a section`
#ASSERT `s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` `A paragraph` `In a subsection` EQUALS `In a subsection`
#ASSERT `s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` `A subparagraph` `In a paragraph` EQUALS `In a paragraph`
#ASSERT `s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` `A clause` `In a subparagraph` EQUALS `In a subparagraph`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` `A Part` `In a section`
        BECAUSE "s 33(3) speaks only of a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 33(3) the section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause is a reference into` `A form` `In a subsection`
        BECAUSE "s 33(3) speaks only of a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause"

-- 33 (4): "a reference ... to regulations is a reference to regulations made under the enactment in which the reference occurs."
#ASSERT `s 33(4) a reference to regulations is a reference to these regulations` "the Land Title Act" "the Land Title Act"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 33(4) a reference to regulations is a reference to these regulations` "the Land Title Act" "the Wills, Estates and Succession Act")

-- 33 (5): "as printed under the King's Printer Act".
#ASSERT `s 33(5) the division or line of the other enactment a reference by number or letter is a reference to` "section 3 (2) (b) as printed" "section 3 (2) (b) in a table of concordance" EQUALS "section 3 (2) (b) as printed"

-- 33 (6): "an Act in that reference includes regulations enacted under the authority of that Act."
#ASSERT `s 33(6) an Act in a reference to a matter under an Act includes the instrument` `The Act itself`
#ASSERT `s 33(6) an Act in a reference to a matter under an Act includes the instrument` `A regulation enacted under the authority of that Act`
-- "includes" is open: a regulation under another Act is not listed, and the text does not say it is left out.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 33(6) an Act in a reference to a matter under an Act includes the instrument` `A regulation enacted under the authority of another Act`
        BECAUSE "s 33(6) says an Act in that reference includes regulations enacted under the authority of that Act; it does not say what else it includes or leaves out"

§ `s 39 and s 40 Definitions borrowed from other Acts`

-- 39: "The definitions section of the Supreme Court Act, so far as the terms defined can be applied, extends to all enactments relating to legal proceedings."
#ASSERT `s 39 the definitions section of the Supreme Court Act extends to the term in the enactment` TRUE TRUE
-- "so far as the terms defined can be applied": a term that cannot be applied is left out, and the words say so.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 39 the definitions section of the Supreme Court Act extends to the term in the enactment` TRUE FALSE)
-- An enactment not relating to legal proceedings is not what the section speaks of.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 39 the definitions section of the Supreme Court Act extends to the term in the enactment` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 39 speaks only of an enactment relating to legal proceedings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 39 the definitions section of the Supreme Court Act extends to the term in the enactment` FALSE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 39 speaks only of an enactment relating to legal proceedings"

-- 40 (1): the Schedule to the Community Charter and section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act apply "so far as the terms defined can be applied" to enactments relating to municipal and regional district matters.
#ASSERT `s 40 the definition applies to the term in the enactment` `The Schedule to the Community Charter` "council" TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 40 the definition applies to the term in the enactment` `Section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act` "board" TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 40 the definition applies to the term in the enactment` `Section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act` "board" FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 40 speaks only of an enactment relating to municipal and regional district matters"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 40 the definition applies to the term in the enactment` `Section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act` "board" TRUE FALSE)
-- 40 (2): "As an exception, subsection (1) does not apply in relation to the definition of "municipality" in the Community Charter."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 40 the definition applies to the term in the enactment` `The Schedule to the Community Charter` "municipality" TRUE TRUE)
-- The exception names the Community Charter's definition only; the Local Government Act's is untouched.
#ASSERT `s 40 the definition applies to the term in the enactment` `Section 1 of the Schedule to the Local Government Act` "municipality" TRUE TRUE

§ `s 42(1) Subdivisions of an Act`

-- "subsections, paragraphs, subparagraphs and clauses", in descending order.
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the place of a subdivision in the descending order` Subsection EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the place of a subdivision in the descending order` Paragraph EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the place of a subdivision in the descending order` Subparagraph EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the place of a subdivision in the descending order` Clause EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the subdivision next below` Subsection EQUALS JUST Paragraph
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the subdivision next below` Paragraph EQUALS JUST Subparagraph
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the subdivision next below` Subparagraph EQUALS JUST Clause
-- Nothing is below a clause.
#ASSERT `s 42(1) the subdivision next below` Clause EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 43 Citation of Acts`

-- (a) and (b): any Act may be cited by chapter number in the volume of its year, or by title.
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `An Act that is neither a revised statute in a general revision nor a limited revision` `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted`
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `A revised statute included in a general revision` `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted`
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `An Act that is a limited revision` `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted`
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `An Act that is neither a revised statute in a general revision nor a limited revision` `By its title, with or without its chapter number`
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `A revised statute included in a general revision` `By its title, with or without its chapter number`
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `An Act that is a limited revision` `By its title, with or without its chapter number`
-- (c): "in the case of an Act that is a revised statute included in a general revision".
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `A revised statute included in a general revision` `By its chapter number in the Revised Statutes of British Columbia`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `An Act that is a limited revision` `By its chapter number in the Revised Statutes of British Columbia`
        BECAUSE "s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed"
-- (d): "in the case of an Act that is a limited revision".
#ASSERT `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `An Act that is a limited revision` `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted and as a Revised Statute of British Columbia for that year`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `A revised statute included in a general revision` `By its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted and as a Revised Statute of British Columbia for that year`
        BECAUSE "s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed"
-- A way the section does not list.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 43 an Act of this kind may be cited this way` `A revised statute included in a general revision` `In some other way`
        BECAUSE "s 43 says only how an Act may be cited; it does not say that another way is not allowed"

§ `s 44 Mutatis mutandis`

-- "If an enactment provides that another enactment applies, it applies with the necessary changes and so far as it is applicable."
#ASSERT `s 44 the other enactment applies` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 44 the other enactment applies` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 44 speaks only of an enactment that provides that another enactment applies"
-- "so far as it is applicable"
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44 the other enactment applies` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 44 the other enactment applies with this change` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44 the other enactment applies with this change` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44 the other enactment applies with this change` FALSE TRUE)
